(3) The cases of prisoners sentenced to more than three years, excepting lifers to whom sub-rule (2)
applies, shall be placed before the Advisory Board if they have served two thirds of their sentence including remission :
Provided that prisoners of the following categories who have been sentenced to imprisonment for more than three years or imprisonment for life shall not be eligible for premature release under the Advisory Board Scheme :-
(i) Prisoners convicted of rape, dacoity, terrorist crimes, offences against the State or prisoners sentenced under section 224, 376, 396 to 400, 402, 467, 471, 472, 474,
489-A, 489-B and 489-D of the Indian Penal Code (Central Act XLV of 1860) ;
